{"id": "EUVD-2026-105097", "enisaUuid": "77b5da6b-f551-3b73-84de-62f284bd917c", "description": "OpenImageIO before 3.0.20.0, 3.1.x before 3.1.15.0, and 3.2.x before 3.2.0.3-beta1 contains an integer overflow in cineon::Codec::Read that undersizes the scanline buffer, causing a heap out-of-bounds read. Attackers can supply a crafted Cineon file with a huge declared width that wraps the size calculation to zero, so UnPackPacked reads past a 4-byte buffer and crashes the application.", "datePublished": "2026-10-20T15:40:41", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-22T09:49:36", "baseScore": 6.8, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:L/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:P/VC:N/VI:N/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/AcademySoftwareFoundation/OpenImageIO/pull/5567", "https://github.com/AcademySoftwareFoundation/OpenImageIO/pull/5568", "https://github.com/AcademySoftwareFoundation/OpenImageIO/commit/07e3c3e0373551c57e7d8e01353deaa4b3646613", "https://github.com/AcademySoftwareFoundation/OpenImageIO/blob/v3.0.19.0/src/cineon.imageio/libcineon/Codec.cpp#L79-L82", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/openimageio-before-3.0.20.0-3.1-x-before-3.1.15.0-and-3.2-x-before-3.2.0.3-beta1-cineon-reader-heap-out-of-bounds-read"], "aliases": ["GHSA-pxpf-24pm-xj4x", "CVE-2026-113681"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.17, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "696b9bc9-981f-3fab-9746-9093b82c0394", "product": {"name": "OpenImageIO", "vendor": {"name": "AcademySoftwareFoundation"}}, "product_version": "0 <3.0.20.0"}, {"id": "d8174560-0ee6-3f83-8669-73a8ea8af6e3", "product": {"name": "OpenImageIO", "vendor": {"name": "AcademySoftwareFoundation"}}, "product_version": "3.1.0.0 <3.1.15.0"}, {"id": "e6c06633-611a-3dcd-a547-7aab1e865164", "product": {"name": "OpenImageIO", "vendor": {"name": "AcademySoftwareFoundation"}}, "product_version": "3.2.0.0-dev <3.2.0.3-beta1"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "8fdbd6ef-9831-329e-9083-ea06aa43419b", "vendor": {"name": "AcademySoftwareFoundation"}}], "isExp